QLC+ input profiles
  Project:   Q Light Controller Plus, https://github.com/mcallegari/qlcplus
  Folder:    resources/inputprofiles
  Commit:    6ed78ed0a697aaa48b1428271e004b22327e5be3
  Copyright: Massimo Callegari, Heikki Junnila and the QLC+ contributors named in each file
  Licence:   Apache License 2.0: see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt

  Where it is:
    packages/midi/profiles/imported/   converted to this project's JSON. Each file says "license": "Apache-2.0" and names
                                       its .qxi and commit in "origin" and "sources".
    packages/midi/profiles/*.json      the three files whose "sources" list a QLC+ input profile took colour tables and LED
                                       values from it (Akai APC40 mkII, Akai APC mini mk2, Novation Launchpad Mini MK3).
    packages/midi/profiles/m-vave-smc-mixer.json
                                       converted like the files in imported/, then corrected after a check on a unit
                                       (issue #7) and given a faceplate, labels and LED values from the unit and its
                                       manual (PR #9). It says "license": "Apache-2.0" and keeps its "origin" and "sources".
    tests/fixtures/qlc/                three .qxi files, unchanged, as test data.
    controllers/<id>/                  files generated from the imported profiles carry the same licence.
    packages/devices/catalog.js        the rows of the imported profiles (id, name, maker, short name) are read off them
                                       and carry the same licence.

  Changes made: read from XML into JSON, numbers decoded into MIDI messages, a generated layout added,
  every control marked "verified": false. Nothing in imported/ has been checked on hardware. The M-VAVE SMC-Mixer was
  checked on a unit by a contributor: its encoders became relative encoders, its layout was drawn from the unit (no longer
  generated), it gained LED feedback and the manual's labels, and its "verifications" says what matched.

Open Fixture Library fixture definitions
  Project:   Open Fixture Library, https://github.com/OpenLightingProject/open-fixture-library
  Folder:    fixtures
  Commit:    849343f6eb7ab64f8d7d93209320bb25a1f5e11d
  Copyright: Florian Edelmann, Felix Edelmann and the Open Fixture Library contributors named in each file
  Licence:   MIT License: see LICENSES/MIT-open-fixture-library.txt

  Where it is:
    tests/fixtures/ofl/                three fixture files, unchanged, as test data.
    packages/dmx/fixtures/imported/    42 fixtures converted by tools/import-ofl.mjs from the files tools/ofl/batch-1.json names,
                                       at the commit above. Each says "license": "MIT" and names its OFL file, commit and authors
                                       in "origin" and "sources" (with the manual and product page the OFL file links to).
    packages/dmx/fixtures/imported-list.js
                                       the id, manufacturer, name, kind and modes of each imported fixture, read off its file.
    packages/devices/catalog.js        the rows of the imported fixtures (id, name, manufacturer, modes) are read off them.
    fixtures/<id>/, zh/fixtures/<id>/  the page of each imported fixture: its channel tables are generated from the converted
                                       file and carry the same licence, with a link to the fixture's page on the Open Fixture
                                       Library.

  Changes made: read into this project's fixture format (open-audiovisual/fixture@1), modes that need 24-bit channels left
  out, wheel slots named after OFL's wheels, every file marked "verified": false. Nothing has been checked on hardware by
  this project.

